  "summary": "All five St. Brigid discharges are reconciled under RBC-TOC-02. Each patient has a progress note. Walter Kim, Terence Stark and Earnest Roberts also have a correction note, because new documents or results came in while I was working.\n\n**Walter Kim**\n- **Furosemide:** changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). The signed addendum corrects the summary's 40 mg daily.\n- **Potassium chloride:** stopped, per the discharge summary.\n- **Omeprazole:** kept. Pantoprazole was only a hospital formulary swap, so I didn't order it.\n- **Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin, aspirin:** no change.\n- **Lisinopril:** first kept on hold, because his 10/21 potassium was 5.4. A repeat panel arrived during the work (10/23: potassium 4.7, creatinine 1.21), which meets the discharge condition, so I resumed it.\n- **Hospital draft addendum (furosemide 60 mg twice daily):** this also arrived. It is unsigned, so I made no change.\n- **Stale task:** your task-t0003 about holding lisinopril no longer applies. I couldn't cancel it from here, so please close it.\n\n**Terence Stark**\n- **Carvedilol:** I first raised it to 12.5 mg twice daily per the summary. A signed addendum then arrived saying the increase was reversed before discharge (heart rate 48–52, lightheaded on standing). His order is now back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016).\n- **Aspirin, insulin 70/30:** no change.\n- **Flagged to you by message:**\n  - **Atorvastatin:** fills covered only 24% of the 180 days before admission (last fill 03/04). I left the order unchanged.\n  - **Glipizide 5 mg:** Dr. Desai at Valley Endocrinology prescribes it and he fills it at Lakeview Drug. There is no clinic order and the summary doesn't mention it. Nothing ordered; please decide whether he should stay on it alongside insulin.\n\n**Earnest Roberts**\n- **Lisinopril:** I resumed it after his post-discharge creatinine (1.08 on 10/22) met the discharge condition, with potassium 4.6. A new potassium of 5.5 on 10/23 then arrived, so I put it back on hold.\n- **Task for you (due 10/26):** review his next potassium before restarting lisinopril.\n- **Insulins, rosuvastatin:** no change.\n\n**Gerald Whitcomb**\n- **Lisinopril:** resumed. Post-discharge creatinine was 1.12 and potassium 4.4 (10/21).\n- **Amlodipine, atorvastatin:** no change.\n- **Still pending:** the potassium the hospital ordered for 3 days after discharge hadn't come in by the time I finished.\n\n**Lorraine Pruitt**\n- **Metformin:** still on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in hospital, which doesn't count toward the post-discharge condition.\n- **Task for you (due 10/24):** review her post-discharge metabolic panel when it arrives and resume metformin if creatinine is under 1.5.\n- **Amlodipine, atorvastatin:** no change.\n\nI closed the four inbox items that arrived during the work. No other new items came in for these patients before I finished.",
